  partName: Exhaust Manifold (3)
  description: The Exhaust Manifold (3) is a medium-sized, compact component located
    at the middle-center-rear of the engine, constructed from plastic-grey material.
    It collects exhaust gases from the cylinders and directs them into the exhaust
    system, playing a crucial role in reducing emissions and improving engine performance.
    Interestingly, the exhaust manifold's design and material help to minimize thermal
    stress and maximize gas flow, contributing to the engine's overall efficiency
    and power output.
